  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds one design record: `docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md`. It has no code. No kernel code starts before the maintainer approves this record.\n\nRevision 2 takes in the maintainer's answers of 2026-11-25:\n- \"Replace the whole motion kernel in one go.\" Scope: 2D milling and 3D Pocket.\n- A side branch and one switch. The program on `main` keeps the old behaviour until the new planner is proven.\n- \"The kernel should be its own crate.\"\n- \"At one point all 40+ motion types should move to the new kernel\".\n\nThe record starts with a \"Plain summary\" that a machinist can read without the code.\n\n## The six stages (plain words)\n\n1. Area: the selection, the side that is material, and the stock and clamps.\n2. Pass shape: rings, rows, a centre line, the line itself, or a helix.\n3. Load control: none, trochoidal loops, or passes that hold the set load. It changes the pass shape only.\n4. Order: the first pass (Inside or Outside) and the cut direction.\n5. Links: the tool stays down. It lifts only with a reason on the status line.\n6. Entry and exit: in air, in a pre-drilled hole, in a cut column, or a helix or ramp only into solid material. Else the operation is refused with a reason.\n\nA strategy is a set of choices for these stages. The stages are a new crate (the crate `camcraft-pathkernel`). It depends only on `camcraft-geometry`, and `camcraft-motion` depends on it.\n\n## The laws as checks\n\nEach law of #4023 has a test shape and a measured value. The stage checks are in the new crate (K7, #4027). The checks of whole programs are in the old-against-new comparison in `camcraft-app`.\n\n## The plan\n\n- First replacement (phase 1): 16 kinds. These are the 2D milling kinds (Thread included), Bore and 3D Pocket.\n- The work is on the side branch `side/path-kernel`. Each sub-PR targets that branch, with one issue each and the normal review rules.\n- `main` is merged into the side branch after each related merge batch, and at least once a week.\n- One switch (old or new) for all 16 kinds. It is old until the proof is complete.\n- The proof: the law suite is green, and the test parts are measured old against new. Each catalog difference has a reason, and the verifier, light and heavy checks are clean. Then one switch-over PR goes to `main`, and the maintainer approves it. A second PR removes the old planners.\n- Defects in the old planners are not patched there. An unsafe one goes to the maintainer as a question.\n- #3750: its golden records of the old output are reused as the baseline. Its move of the old code on `main` is dropped.\n- Roadmap: all 49 kinds in six phases (turning is phase 3). The record has a fit check of each later family and names what does not fit (tool tilt, a surface guide, the lathe plane, the two wire guides, cycles with no path, the sinker orbit). It also lists what phase 1 keeps open.\n\n## Answered by the maintainer, 2026-11-25\n\nThe maintainer approved the design: \"Yes, start\". No question is open.\n- The crate name is `camcraft-pathkernel`.\n- Phase 1 has 16 kinds: Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset, Engrave, V-Carve, 2D Chamfer, Circular, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Trace, Slot Undercut, Thread, Bore and 3D Pocket.\n- The phases: 1 is the first replacement; 2 is sheet cutting, Drill and Probe; 3 is turning (\"Lathe earlier\", then \"Third\"); 4 is 3D Finish and Deburr; 5 is wire and sinker; 6 is multi-axis and rotary.\n- A \"Side branch\" rule goes into AGENTS.md first, and `side/path-kernel` is protected.\n- The heavy `motion` and `app` steps run one time on the side branch before the switch-over.\n- The maintainer reads the list of changed programs and approves the switch-over PR.\n- One issue each for the five kinds with no issue: #4034 V-Carve, #4035 Slot, #4036 Trochoidal slot, #4037 Slot Undercut, #4038 Thread.\n\nThe work plane and the tool shape stay open from the start, because turning is phase 3.\n\n## Tests\n\nNone. This is a docs-only PR. No build ran, and no gate is necessary.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #4024\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
